            <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="1" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="2" />
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The air leakage of the house is very high. We notice infiltration from the followings house components:



- Attic hatch: Small but because is located in the bathroom some humidity can cross into the attic and creating condensation. This situation is favorable for formation of mould. We recommend to use weather strips to seal the attic hatch or even if possible to close it permanently and putting the access outside.

- Windows: All skylights, the kitchen and the dinning room, master bedroom and the bedrooms windows.

- Door: The garage door (inside door), the door in the staircase leading to the basement

- Electric panel: In the laundry room and in the staircase leading to the basement

- Receptacles

- Wood stove and fireplace

- Furnace combustion air supply damper



Sealing the house will contribute to better managed the temperature of the house, it has also a direct impact on your energy consumption.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>We recommend to add insulation on the exterior walls to meet the actual standard or a minmum of R-20 to be eligible to the rebate. Min. R-20; $2.50/SQUARE FOOT

                  Min. R-30: $3.50/SQUARE FOOT



We recommend the insulation from the ouside part of the wall, because it gives the opportunity to seal the building properly, it avoid the reduction of space inside, reduce the disagreement of the renovations inside and reduce.</mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>We recommend the adidtion of insulation of the roof to meet the actual standard of R-60.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>We recommend the insulation of the uninsulated part of the basement (mechanical room).</foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows with ENERGY STAR and ZONE 3 certified windows. The seal of some window is broken and therfore not protecting the windows against the air passing through the unit.</windows>
                <HeatingSystem>During the evauation the owner mention the idea of replacing the actual oil furnace by an electric furnace. We recommend to do so for the following reasons:

- 100% efficient

- No combustion gases

- No risk of combustion gases back draf

- Doesn't make any pollution

- It's safe</HeatingSystem>
                <WaterConservation>We recommend the replacement of he 13L toilet for a low flow units. It will contribute to reduce the consumption of water</WaterConservation>
                <AdditionalComments>The house is actually under partial renovation due to a flood. Material containing asbestos have been found on the drywall joints compound and heating duct insulation sheet. Be careful in presence of these products. All type of renovation muct be planned in a way to reduce the risk of exposition of asbestos fibres.

</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
